package CodeList
import Trigger
import ErrorHandling

/*	CodeList

	An ordered list of `code` values that is run in one go, in the thread that runs it. It behaves like the
	conditions of a trigger, without the engine round trip on Lua.

	Jass cannot keep a `code` value in an array or a class field, so a library that wants to call a set of
	registered callbacks keeps a trigger and evaluates it. On Jass that is what a CodeList is. On Lua it costs
	the engine's round trip on every dispatch, measured on the 3.0.0 client at about 3.3 us per listener where
	a call costs about 0.13 us, so the Lua backend lowers the three functions below to one table per list, an
	append, and a loop of calls.

	This needs a compiler with that lowering. The Jass bodies below are what runs on Jass, and on Lua a build
	whose compiler does not know the lowering would silently pay the trigger round trip on every event, so
	there the bodies fail at the first list created instead.

	The functions are recognised by the compiler through their annotation and their exact signatures, so they
	must keep these shapes. They stay private to this package: a list is used through the class.

	What a list promises, on both targets, and what is measured in the game against a trigger:
	- The code runs in the order it was added, once per run.
	- It runs like a trigger condition, in the current thread. It must not wait.
	- The result of a callback is ignored: the game runs every condition after one that returned false.
	- Code added while the list runs is reached in the same run.
	- A callback that fails does not stop the ones after it.
*/

// Jass state: the trigger behind each list. Lua does not touch it.
trigger array listTriggers
var listCount = 0

function requireLowering()
	if isLua
		error("CodeList needs a compiler that lowers the codeList intrinsics to Lua; update the compiler.")

/** Creates an empty list. It lives as long as the map does. */
@compilerintrinsic function codeListCreate() returns int
	requireLowering()
	listTriggers[listCount] = CreateTrigger()
	listCount++
	return listCount - 1

/** Adds code to the end of the list. */
@compilerintrinsic function codeListAdd(int list, code c)
	requireLowering()
	listTriggers[list].addCondition(Condition(c))

/** Runs every code value of the list, in the order added. */
@compilerintrinsic function codeListRun(int list)
	requireLowering()
	listTriggers[list].evaluate()

public class CodeList
	private int list

	construct()
		list = codeListCreate()

	/** Adds code to the end of the list. */
	function add(code c)
		codeListAdd(list, c)

	/** Runs every code value of the list, in the order added, in the current thread. It must not wait. */
	function run()
		codeListRun(list)
